<title>UK: BGB Finance sets 1.5 bln French franc 12-year bond.</title>
<headline>BGB Finance sets 1.5 bln French franc 12-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond was announced by joint lead managers Caisse des Depots et Consignations and J.P. Morgan.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BGB FINANCE</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  BANKGESELLSCHAFT BERLIN GROUP</p>
<p> AMT    1.5 BLN FFR   COUPON     5.75	MATURITY    20.MAR.09</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  100.386   PAY DATE    20.MAR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  2.00	REOFFER    98.736    SPREAD	+38 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AA1	 LISTING    PARIS     PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> IBCA	 AAA     DENOMS (K) 10-100-1M SALE LIMITS US/UK/FR/DE</p>
<p> NEG PLG    YES	 CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   YES</p>
<p> GOV LAW    ENGLISH   HOME CTRY  =	   TAX PROVS   =</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.35	SELL CONC  1.65	PRAECIPUUM  =</p>
<p> UNDERLYING GOVT BOND INTERPOLATED 8.50 PCT 2008 OAT AND 6.50</p>
<p>			    PCT 2011 OAT</p>
<p> NOTES	ISSUED OFF THE EMTN PROGRAMME</p>
<p>		SUBORDINATED</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
